[Music]  a new report says an autopsy concluded  that carbon monoxide poisoning led to  the deaths of three american tourists at  a sandals resort in the bahamas earlier  this month the victim's family is now  asking for a second independent autopsy  in their search for answers here to  weigh in fox news contributor dr marty  mccary doc should the families of the  victims be satisfied with this report or  should they be skeptical and want a  second autopsy  well they should be a little skeptical  that toxicology reports have actually  not been released they should ask to see  them but we do know that carbon monoxide  poisoning does kill about 400 to 500  people a year and it is something that  does happen and there may be a plausible  mechanism if you put all the pieces  together in the circumstances of what  happened yeah i'm trying to figure that  out trying to visualize a standard hotel  room where would carbon monoxide come  out of the various things that are in a  hotel room my first instinct is the  heater air conditioner but anywhere else  i mean it's possible that a gas oven or  range could release carbon monoxide it  could be that there's a garage where  cars are parked within the building and  perhaps a channel by which that gas  could go into the room so those are all  possibilities when you heard that  pesticide theory from people in the  hotel saying they smelt a strong smell  of pesticide carbon monoxide has no  smell pesticide obviously in many cases  does  would you travel down that path and do a  little bit more research on the  pesticide angle because to me if other  people were smelling that that could be  cause for concern at least in my  estimation  that's right look that's a very good  point todd and i think you have to  assume it's an environmental exposure  until proven otherwise carbon monoxide  is classically odorless  and a colorless gas so you would not  expect any odor so the pieces really  right now don't fit together  if they had called for help like they  did i mean they weren't feeling real  great they went inside got some  treatment could they have been saved or  at some point is your body just so  compromised that nothing can be done  once carbon monoxide enters your system  well first of all carbon monoxide  poisoning does  act really quickly people  within a matter of minutes can lose  consciousness and the treatment is  pretty simple get people to a better air  source so it is possible that even a  matter of seconds could have made a big  difference in trying to help these  individuals a complete tragedy so many  answered unanswered questions still at  this point meantime you are calling out  a cdc advisory panel for approving covet  boosters for kids as pfizer is looking  to jab kids as young as six months why  are you coming out so strongly against  this panel doc  well again the biden administration's  fda was completely bypassed in convening  their technical experts their advisory  committee these are the top vaccine  experts in the country many had signaled  that they're not on board with this  recommendation to  uh give a booster to 24 million five  through 11 year olds and so when you  make such a sweeping recommendation for  the entire country with such strong  vigor  ordering all 24 million children in the  country 5 through 11 to get a booster  you should convene your technical  experts instead  they put it in front of a cdc committee  which is well known to fire people who  have dissenting opinions they did that  with dr martin called cold door from  harvard last year  and the  conversation was incredible there was no  clinical data to support the booster for  five through eleven-year-olds instead  they cited a small study done by pfizer  of 140 children in that age group  looking at no outcomes but instead the  antibody bump you get after the booster  and the committee actually said we want  a simple message we're concerned about  having a confusing message if these kids  are not getting a booster and older  people are that is not a scientific  rationale  it doesn't make a lot of sense doc you  gave a great explanation there we  appreciate it dr marty mccary we'll see  what happens with both of these stories  thank you sir  subscribe to the fox news youtube  channel to catch our nightly opens  stories that are changing the world and  changing your life from tucker carlson  tonight

